          "filename": "Compton Bishop, Cross - geograph.org.uk - 43850.jpg",
          "caption": "Compton Bishop: Cross. Cross was a key posting station in coaching days. Two inns survive  the White Hart, seen here, and the New Inn. The White Hart, but probably not this structure, was extant at the time of the Monmouth Rebellion in 1685 and the subsequent Bloody Assizes and the inn is said to be haunted by one of Judge Jefferies victims. The A38 trunk road now bypasses the village",
